<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magar people</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Magars</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Magars are one of the largest indigenous peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, living mainly in the western and central hills. Speakers of Tibeto-Burman Magar languages, they formed a large part of the army with which the Gorkha kingdom unified Nepal in the eighteenth century and have long been recruited into the Gurkha regiments of the British and Indian armies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magar-people.jpg" alt="Magar people" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MagarUK · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Magar_Cultural_Dress.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
